# Every variable this app reads is listed here, and every one of them is
# resolved and checked in lib/env.ts. A production build refuses to start on a
# configuration that would take money and lose it; see the boot log.

# --- Store (required in production) ---
# Without both of these, every serverless instance keeps its own clock and
# ledger, and a payment lands on whichever instance answered the webhook.
# A production build will refuse to start.
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=

# --- Payments: all three, or none ---
# Two out of three is the shape that takes money it cannot credit, so a build
# with a partial set refuses to start in every environment.
# With none of them set, the site runs and refuses every payment.
POLAR_ACCESS_TOKEN=
POLAR_PRODUCT_ID=
POLAR_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# "sandbox" or "production". Anything else is treated as production.
POLAR_SERVER=production

# --- Site ---
# Absolute http(s) URL. Used for metadata and for the checkout return.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://lastlight.lol
# Omit to send no analytics at all. Read at runtime, so it can be set without
# a rebuild.
NEXT_PUBLIC_OPENPANEL_CLIENT_ID=
# Where those events go. Omit for OpenPanel's hosted cloud; set it to the API
# origin of a self-hosted instance to keep the data yourself. It is the API
# host, not the dashboard: https://api-openpanel.example.com. Spelled any other
# way it is silently ignored and the events go to the cloud, so the boot check
# names near misses rather than let that pass.
NEXT_PUBLIC_OPENPANEL_API_URL=
# Where the SDK script itself is loaded from. Omit to load it from openpanel.dev
# even when the events are self-hosted. A self-hosted instance serves it from
# the DASHBOARD origin, not the API one, and the path matters:
# https://openpanel.example.com/op1.js. An origin on its own puts HTML in a
# script tag and analytics never starts, so that is warned about too.
NEXT_PUBLIC_OPENPANEL_SCRIPT_URL=

# --- Clock ---
# Unix MILLISECONDS of the launch instant, pinned at deploy so a cold start an
# hour in does not hand the site a fresh 24 hours. Unset means the clock starts
# at the first read, which is what you want locally. A seconds value here puts
# the launch in 1970 and the site is born dead, so that mistake is warned about.
CLOCK_LAUNCH_AT=

# --- Demo instances only ---
# "1" marks this instance as a demo: the checkout applies payments directly
# instead of refusing them, and the missing-Redis check drops to a warning.
# On a live site this means anyone can move the clock and take the Last Light
# for free. It exists for screenshots.
ALLOW_SIMULATED_PAYMENTS=
